        "text": "Next, you may have noticed that the terms coin and token seem to be used interchangeably sometimes. But are coins and tokens the same thing? At first glance, coins and tokens appear similar. Both exist on blockchains, can be traded on exchanges, and sent between crypto wallets. But the biggest difference is that coins are the native asset of a blockchain, such as Bitcoin on the Bitcoin network, Ether on the Ethereum network, and BNB on the BNB chain, whereas tokens are built on top of existing blockchains. For example, there are many tokens built based on the popular ERC20 token standard, but there is only one native coin, ether on the Ethereum network. Moreover, tokens can be used like cryptocurrencies, but they are more flexible. They can serve as anything from digital receipts representing a stake in a company to loyalty points.",
        "start": 560,
        "end": 52400,
